# British English Localisation Rule

All documentation in this project shall be in British English.

This includes:
- Spelling conventions (e.g., "colour" instead of "color", "organise" instead of "organize")
- Terminology (e.g., "behaviour" instead of "behavior", "recognise" instead of "recognize")
- Date formats (DD/MM/YYYY preferred over MM/DD/YYYY where applicable)
- Consistent use of British English throughout all project documentation, code comments, and communications

Agents shall apply British English standards when creating or modifying any textual content in the project.
